## [x] 2. Resolve the huqan/axiom namespace before the internal-tool lookup
Commit 09a2b3b.
- huqan.policy answered external/block/unknown-tool-blocked for huqan.learn and
  internal/allow for learn. INTERNAL_TOOLS holds bare names; mcpServer.js
  advertises huqan.*.
- Fixed by resolving the namespace at lookup, not by enlarging INTERNAL_TOOLS
  (agent.js aliases it as ALLOWED_TOOLS, so growing it is a capability change).

## [x] 3. Close the HTTP ingest loop
Commit 8400e4e.
Root cause was neither of the two things it looked like from the HTTP surface.
plugins/company-brain.js::addCompanyEdge never passed `strength`, and
graph.js::addEdge refuses a causal relation without one by throwing. Manual and
decision ingest therefore died on all four advertised causal relations, after
proposeNode had already written the endpoints -- hence orphan nodes, no edges,
and verify answering unknown.

INGEST_EXECUTION_UNKNOWN turned out to be correct rather than a second defect:
classifyActionOutcome() refused to call `result.ok !== true` a bounded success.
It reports admission_allow_graph_write_observed now that the outcome is bounded.
Fixed by centralising the rule in lib/causal-edge-strength.js.

## [x] 4. Flip MCP verify to the canonical English status vocabulary
huqan.verify answers {"status":"bilinmiyor"} while REST /verify answers
{"status":"unknown"}. It is the last Turkish string on a surface every Claude
and Cursor user sees.

Not an oversight: lib/mcp/response-builders.js:258 projects the envelope back
through toLegacyVerifyEnvelope() on purpose, because mcpServer.js VERIFY_STATUS
is an advertised output schema and a wire contract. Both directions of the
adapter already exist in lib/verify-status-vocabulary.js.

Done. HUQAN_MCP_LEGACY_VERIFY_STATUS=1 retains the legacy enum for a client
that has not migrated, and moves the advertised schema and the emitted payload
together so a client reading the schema it is given is correct in either mode.
Acceptance of both spellings on the way in is unchanged and permanent.

